====================================================================
PolyKernel T36 Wave 7: Dataflow task model + scheduler
  3 task types: data (wavelet-triggered, bound to a color /
  data_task_id), local (self-triggered via @activate), control.
  Rendezvous @activate/@block/@unblock: a task runs ONLY when
  activated AND unblocked. A compute task (a data task bound to TWO
  input colors) fires only after BOTH input wavelets arrive (the
  dataflow rendezvous). TaskPicker selects a runnable task. Builds
  on the Todo 35 core (Color/Wavelet/Router/Grid wavelet arrival).
  NOTE: a GPU-free functional/cycle SIMULATOR - does NOT compile real
  CSL and does NOT run on Cerebras hardware. No @compute/@data
  decorators (compute is an exported host-callable convention).
Evidence: ctest -R scheduler (compute fires only after both wavelets
          arrive; block/unblock gates firing; data fires on wavelet
          arrival; local fires on activate; task picker).
====================================================================

